{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`project.review-phase-boundaries` runs advisory. `.rebar/criteria_routing.json:82-87` holds\n`\"default_posture\": \"advisory\"`, `\"block_threshold\": 0.9`, `\"blocking_enabled\": false`.\n\nThe sampling already recorded on this ticket (2026-08-05) covered 51 in-scope reviews and found 6\nfindings with a maximum author impact of **0.5**, against a 0.90 block threshold. That measurement\nsettles one thing decisively: **flipping `blocking_enabled` at the current 0.90 threshold would\nchange nothing** — no observed finding has ever come within 0.4 of the line. So \"enable blocking\"\nand \"keep advisory\" are not the real choice; the real choice is what threshold, if any, makes this\ncriterion load-bearing without punishing authors.\n\n**Operator direction (2026-08-09):** do not pick a posture from the current sample. First assess the\nHISTORICAL IMPACT of lowering the threshold — i.e. counter-factually replay what would have been\nblocked at candidate thresholds — and choose from that evidence.\n\nA caveat carried forward from the existing sampling comment, which the analysis must resolve rather\nthan inherit: the 6 findings were never confirmed against false positives. A threshold chosen from\na finding set that includes false positives would block authors on reviewer noise.\n\nRelated and directly instructive: ticket `f391`'s analysis of the `undecomposed` axis showed that\nthis codebase's persisted `*-REVIEW_RESULT.json` sidecar stream under `.tickets-tracker/` supports\nexactly this kind of counter-factual replay at **zero LLM cost**, and that an impact floor applied\nwithout regard to grade silently makes a low-graded finding block like a high-graded one. Use the\nsame replay instrument here, and check for the same failure mode.\n\n## Plan\n\nReplay the persisted review corpus and, for each candidate `block_threshold`, compute what WOULD\nhave blocked: how many changes, on which tickets, and with what author-visible impact scores. Then\naudit the findings that a candidate threshold would newly make blocking — every one of them — for\nfalse positives, since those are precisely the cases that would have stopped an author.\n\nReport the trade-off curve rather than a single number, then record a posture decision (threshold\nvalue and `blocking_enabled`) justified by that curve.\n\nDo NOT change `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` in this ticket. Landing a routing/posture change is a\nseparate reviewable change, and coupling the analysis to the config edit would make the evidence\nhard to review on its own merits.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis is an analysis ticket: its deliverable is a recorded readout, not code. Verification is that\nthe numbers are reproducible — state the corpus location, the replay method, and the exact\ndenominator, so a second reader can re-derive the curve. Never estimate a rate whose denominator is\nnot reachable from the checkout; say so instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The counter-factual replay is recorded: for each candidate `block_threshold`, the number of\n      reviews and distinct tickets that would have been blocked, with the corpus size and the exact\n      denominator stated.\n- [ ] Every finding that a candidate threshold would newly make BLOCKING is audited for false\n      positives, and the false-positive rate among them is reported.\n- [ ] The readout states whether impact is applied grade-independently for this criterion (the\n      failure mode `f391` found on the `undecomposed` axis), since a grade-independent floor would\n      make any threshold choice misleading.\n- [ ] A posture decision is recorded — threshold value and whether `blocking_enabled` flips —\n      justified by the curve and the false-positive audit, not by the 51-review sample alone.\n- [ ] The readout has a Limits section separating verified observations from what the reachable\n      corpus could not answer.\n- [ ] `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` is UNCHANGED by this ticket; any posture change is filed as a\n      separate follow-up ticket linked `discovered_from`.","title":"Assess historical impact of lowering the project.review-phase-boundaries block threshold"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786326471559688001,"uuid":"1ca6bd1f-eb2a-4e64-8655-888744587579"}